Now, you know we had
science Mike McHargue,

01:09:17.080 --> 01:09:20.000
our really good friend on GMM recently

01:09:20.000 --> 01:09:22.913
for the leaving things in citric acid.

01:09:23.990 --> 01:09:24.823
And,

01:09:26.620 --> 01:09:29.040
both of us talked
extensively about his book

01:09:29.040 --> 01:09:30.613
on our social medias.

01:09:32.460 --> 01:09:33.560
Because...

01:09:35.430 --> 01:09:37.290
I'm not exaggerating, and
I'm not just saying this

01:09:37.290 --> 01:09:39.883
because Mike is a
friend, but this book is,

01:09:40.830 --> 01:09:44.209
I think very timely, given the fact that

01:09:44.209 --> 01:09:47.100
there's an opportunity for
introspection right now,

01:09:47.100 --> 01:09:48.169
you're spending a lot of time
Well, with ourselves

01:09:48.169 --> 01:09:49.370
is a lie.
With yourself.

01:09:49.370 --> 01:09:50.203
You're always with--
With yourself.

01:09:50.203 --> 01:09:52.860
Yourself but you're not...

01:09:52.860 --> 01:09:55.300
We're sitting with ourselves a lot more.

01:09:55.300 --> 01:09:58.070
And I think things are
coming up, it's like what?

01:09:58.070 --> 01:09:59.070
Why am I feeling this?

01:09:59.070 --> 01:10:01.320
Why am I acting this way?

01:10:01.320 --> 01:10:03.740
And a lot of those questions are answered

01:10:05.809 --> 01:10:09.917
in a benevolent way, so
you can be kind to yourself

01:10:10.770 --> 01:10:12.270
as you begin to understand--
Yeah.

01:10:12.270 --> 01:10:14.495
Parts of yourself that
you didn't previous.

01:10:14.495 --> 01:10:17.220
I mean, the one of the reasons I love Mike

01:10:17.220 --> 01:10:19.540
and I love this book is

01:10:19.540 --> 01:10:24.540
he approaches things with
like diligently researched

01:10:25.160 --> 01:10:30.120
scientific standpoint and it's not...

01:10:30.120 --> 01:10:33.450
There's no whoo in this is, it is like,

01:10:33.450 --> 01:10:37.170
this is stuff that is factual and true.

01:10:37.170 --> 01:10:39.490
It's not some fluffy self-help thing.

01:10:39.490 --> 01:10:44.490
It's like, this is what
science tells us about people.

01:10:44.690 --> 01:10:49.690
And this is how those facts
about people and humanity

01:10:49.710 --> 01:10:52.400
translate into you and your tendencies,

01:10:52.400 --> 01:10:53.590
both good and bad.

01:10:53.590 --> 01:10:58.100
And it's extremely compassionate
and non-judgmental.

01:10:58.100 --> 01:10:58.933
I think,

01:10:59.890 --> 01:11:00.990
you could

01:11:02.490 --> 01:11:03.323
reading a book,

01:11:03.323 --> 01:11:05.793
understand why you're a pain your own ass,

01:11:09.820 --> 01:11:12.893
it could be indicting, but
he has a great way of it.

01:11:13.922 --> 01:11:15.870
And this is who he is, as a person,

01:11:15.870 --> 01:11:18.540
it's like, he's loving and accepting it.

01:11:18.540 --> 01:11:22.360
And that translates into
how you process yourself,

01:11:22.360 --> 01:11:23.600
which is very powerful.

01:11:23.600 --> 01:11:25.090
And a lot of times you don't know

01:11:25.090 --> 01:11:26.790
that you're a pain in the ass to yourself.

01:11:26.790 --> 01:11:29.330
You're just mad, you're
mad at everybody else,

01:11:29.330 --> 01:11:30.580
you're mad at yourself.

01:11:30.580 --> 01:11:32.750
And you haven't even
stopped a process like,

01:11:32.750 --> 01:11:37.093
oh, if I take a one step back
and get perspective on this,

01:11:38.180 --> 01:11:41.480
that anger a lot of times
will just kinda melt away

01:11:41.480 --> 01:11:42.810
when you gain perspective.

